$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
1,4-Bis[dialkyl(2,3,4,5-tetrabromo-2-pentenyl)-ammonio]-2-butene
dibromides IIIa-IIId. A tenfold molar excess of bromine was added
dropwise with continuous stirring at room temperature to an aqueous
solution of 0.03 mol of Ia-Id. After 4 h the resulting complex was washed
with five 50-ml portions of water and dried. Decomposition of the
complexes with acetone (chemically pure grade) yielded compounds
IIIa-IIId, which were recrystallized from diethyl ether. Compound IIIc
Yield: 100%. mp: 107-108 °C; R f: 0.46; IR spectrum, ν, cm-1: 570, 1605,
1615; UV spectrum, λmax,nm: 232; Formula: C28H44Br10N2; ; 1H NMR
spectrum, δ, ppm (J, Hz)a: 1.00 t (12H, NCH2CH2CH3, J 8.0), 1.90 m (8H,
NCH2CH2CH3), 3.44 m (8H, NCH2C2H5), 3.92 m and 3.96 m (4H, CH2Br), 4.38
br.d (4H, CH2CH=, J -5.5), 4.70 and 4.90 d.d (4H, CH2CBr=, Jgem15.0),
5.80 d.d (2H, CHBr, J 1 10.8, J 2 5.7), 6.64 br.t (2H, CH=CH, J -5.5)
