$DATUM 1,4-Bis[dialkyl(2,3,4,5-tetrabromo-2-pentenyl)-ammonio]-2-butene
dibromides IIIa-IIId. A tenfold molar excess of bromine was added
dropwise with continuous stirring at room temperature to an aqueous
solution of 0.03 mol of Ia-Id. After 4 h the resulting complex was washed
with five 50-ml portions of water and dried. Decomposition of the
complexes with acetone (chemically pure grade) yielded compounds
IIIa-IIId, which were recrystallized from diethyl ether. Compound IIIa
mp: 128-129 °C; R f: 0.48; IR spectrum, ν, cm-1: 570, 1605, 1615; UV
spectrum, λmax,nm: 233; Formula: C18H28Br10N2; 1H NMR spectrum, δ, ppm
(J, Hz)a: 3.31 s and 3.34 s (12H, NCH3), 3.94 m and 3.97 m (4H, CH2Br),
4.48 br.d (4H, CH2CH=, J -5.5), 4.71 and 4.90 d.d (4H, CH2CBr=,
Jgem15.0), 5.80 d.d (2H, CHBr, J 1 10.8, J 2 5.7), 6.60 br.t (2H, CH=CH,
J -5.5).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of
1,4-bis[dialkyl(2,3,4,5-tetrabromo-2-pentenyl)ammonio]-2-butene
dibromides
