$DATUM β-Hexabromo-meso-tris(4-tert-butylphenyl)subporphyrin (4c) From
subporphyrin 2c (70 mg, 106 μmol), chromatography (CH2Cl2-PE-Et2O,
1:8:1), to give 4c (120 mg, 100%) as a yellow solid. 1H NMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3, -40 °C): δ = 8.02 (d, J = 7.80 Hz, 3 H, o-HPh), 7.74 (d, J = 7.80
Hz, 3 H, m-HPh), 7.49 (d, J = 7.80 Hz, 3 H, m-HPh), 7.16 (d, J = 7.80 Hz,
3 H, o-HPh), 1.48 (s, 27 H, t-Bu). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 152.74,
134.44, 132.38, 130.86, 128.74, 124.55, 120.32, 118.32, 34.91, 31.59. 19F
NMR (376 MHz, CDCl3): δ = -157.10 (m, 1 F, BF). HRMS (MALDI TOF): m/z
[M-F]+ calcd for C45H39BN3Br6: 1104.8368; found: 1104.8399. UV/Vis
(CH2Cl2): λ (relative intensity) = 374 (26), 458 nm (3.75). Fluorescence
(in CH2Cl2, λex = 374 nm): λmax = 521 nm, ΦF = 0.001.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
