$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Method A To a vigorously stirred solution of
dry ZnBr2 (1.13 g, 5 mmol) in CHCl3 (25 mL) was added Pb(OAc)4 (1.11 g,
2.5 mmol). Stirring continued for 5 min while a solution of the alkene or
the alkyne (2 mmol) in CHCl3 (5 mL) was added all at once. The mixture
was stirred for the specified reaction time and then filtered by suction.
The filtrate was washed with aqueous sodium metabisulfite and water. It
was dried (Na2SO4) and evaporated in vacuo to give the dibromide. The
yields were measured by GC and H NMR. 1,2-Dibromophenylethane, yield 92%.
Mp. °C, or bp. °C/torr: Found, 72-74; Lit. 74-75[20]
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Mild oxidative bromination of alkenes and alkynes with zinc bromide and
lead tetraacetate
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Muathen, Hussni A.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2004), 34(19), 3545-3552

