$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Bromination of ammonium salts Ia-Id,
IIIa-IIId, V, and VI. To aqueous solution of 0.03 mol of salt Ia-Id,
IIIa-IIId, V, or VI we added dropwise at room temperature with constant
stirring a 10- or 5-fold molar amount of bromine. After 4 h, the complex
that formed was washed with water (5 x 50 ml) and dried. Decomposition
with acetone (chemical grade) gave compound IIa-IId, IVa-g, VII, or VIII
as hygroscopic oily or crystalline substances. They were recrystallized
from absolute ethanol. Comp. no.: VIII, Yield: 99%. Rf : 0.45, IR
spectrum, v, cm-1: 590, 1605, 1615, UV spectrum, λmax, nm: 225, Formula:
Cl9H35Br6ClN2. 1H NMR spectrum [CD3OD or (CD3)2SO], δ, ppm (J, Hz): 1.39
t and 1.50 t (15H, CH2CH3, J 8.0), 3.65 q and 3.69 q (10H, CH2CH3), 3.93
m and 4.14 m (2H, CH2Br), 4.24 d (2H, CH2CH=, J 4.2), 4.38 s (2H.
CH2CCl=), 4.69 d.d and 4.90 d.d (2H, CH2CBr=, J 15.0), 5.80 d.d (1H,
CHBr, J 1 10.8, J 2 5.7), 6.45 br.t (1H, CH=CCl, J 5.5)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Bromination of mono- and bisammonium salts with a 4-penten-2-ynyl side
group
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
