$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Yield 99%, our studies began with the acetal 3, readily available from
2,3-butanedione and easily converted to the enol ether 4.5 After some
experimentation, we found that this compound could be brominated to
afford the sensitive dibromide 5 (Scheme 2). While this compound was too
sensitive for long-term storage, we found that freshly prepared 5 engaged
in 4+3 cycloaddition chemistry.6
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Vinyl oxo carbenium ions in 4+3 cycloadditions. Bromination of an alkoxy
enone, cycloaddition chemistry of the adduct and chemistry of the
cycloadducts
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Harmata, Michael; Rashatasakhon, Paitoon
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synlett (2000), (10), 1419-1422

