$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for the reaction between DHAs 1a,b,d-1g and bromine for
the formation of known 2-aryl-7,8-dibromo-DHAs in CS2 To a stirred
solution of DHA 1a,b,d-g (0.50 mmol) in CS2 (20 mL) under an argon
atmosphere, excluded from light, a solution of Br2 in CS2 (0.50 mmol,
0.78 M) was added dropwise. The reaction was monitored by TLC and after
completed reaction (approximately 20 min) a sample (0.5 mL) from the
reaction vessel was transferred to an NMR-tube together with CDCl3 (0.5
mL). 1H NMR data were in agreement with those from literature.15
2-(4′-Nitrophenyl)-7,8-dibromo-7,8,1,8a-tetrahydroazulene-1,1-dicarbonitrile
(2a) 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3/CS2 (1:1)) δ 8.34 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H), 7.91
(d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H), 7.14 (s, 1H), 6.41 (d, J = 7.3 Hz, 1H), 6.15 (dd, J
= 12.1, 7.3 Hz, 1H), 6.02 (dd, J = 12.1, 5.0 Hz, 1H), 5.35-5.29 (m, 1H),
5.06-5.01 (m, 1H), 4.69 (s, 1H) ppm.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM in the dark, alternative reaction conditions gave lower yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM On the Solvent-Dependent Bromination of Dihydroazulenes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Kilde, Martin Droehse; Broman, Soeren Lindbaek; Kadziola, Anders;
Nielsen, Mogens Broendsted
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synlett (2016), 27(3), 450-454

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME62 STEP1
$RXN



