$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-(4'-Nitrophenyl)-7,8-dibromo-7,8,1,8a-tetrahydroazulene-1,1-dicarbonitrile
(10.1). To a stirred solution of DHA 1.1 (143 mg, 0.473 mmol) in CH2Cl2
(5 mL) under an argon atmosphere at -78 °C was added a solution of Br2 in
CH2Cl2 (0.61 mL, 0.78 M, 0.47 mmol) dropwise. The brown mixture was then
stirred for 30 min, after which the solution took a yellow color.
Evaporation of the solvents gave dibromide 10.1. Yellow solid, yield 218
mg, 0.47 mmol, >99%. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.35 (d, J = 9.0 Hz, 2H),
7.91 (d, J = 9.0 Hz, 2H), 7.15 (s, 1H), 6.42 (dd, J = 7.5, 2.3 Hz, 1H),
6.13 (dd, J = 12.2, 7.5 Hz, 1H), 6.00 (dd, J = 12.2, 5.6 Hz, 1H),
5.32-5.30 (m, 1H), 5.05-5.04 (m, 1H), 4.70 (br s, 1H) ppm. 13C NMR (125
MHz, CDCl3) δ 148.3, 143.9, 137.9, 137.1, 136.0, 130.2, 127.2, 125.5,
124.8, 123.9, 114.2, 111.3, 53.3, 51.0, 48.9, 44.6 ppm. Anal. Calcd for
C18H13N3O2 (303.31): C, 46.89; H, 2.40; N, 9.11. Found: C, 46.94; H,
2.31; N, 8.82.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, Br2 added dropwise
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Syntheses of Donor-Acceptor-Functionalized Dihydroazulenes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Broman, Soeren Lindbaek; Jevric, Martyn; Bond, Andrew D.; Nielsen, Mogens
Broendsted
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2014), 79(1), 41-64

