$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the reaction between
DHAs 1a,b,d-1g and bromine for the formation of known
2-aryl-7,8-dibromo-DHAs in CS2 To a stirred solution of DHA 1a,b,d-g
(0.50 mmol) in CS2 (20 mL) under an argon atmosphere, excluded from
light, a solution of Br2 in CS2 (0.50 mmol, 0.78 M) was added dropwise.
The reaction was monitored by TLC and after completed reaction
(approximately 20 min) a sample (0.5 mL) from the reaction vessel was
transferred to an NMR-tube together with CDCl3 (0.5 mL). 1H NMR data were
in agreement with those from literature.15
2-(4′-Cyanophenyl)-7,8-dibromo-7,8,1,8a-tetrahydroazulene-1,1-dicarbonitrile
(2b) 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3/CS2 (1:1)) δ 7.85 (d, J = 8.6 Hz, 2H), 7.77
(d, J = 8.6 Hz, 2H), 7.10 (s, 1H), 6.38 (dd, J = 7.5, 1.9 Hz, 1H), 6.13
(dd, J = 12.3, 7.5 Hz, 1H), 5.99 (dd, J = 12.3, 5.4 Hz, 1H), 5.31 (s,
1H), 5.04 (s, 1H), 4.68 (s, 1H) ppm.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM in the dark, alternative reaction conditions gave lower yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM On the Solvent-Dependent Bromination of Dihydroazulenes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Kilde, Martin Droehse; Broman, Soeren Lindbaek; Kadziola, Anders;
Nielsen, Mogens Broendsted
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synlett (2016), 27(3), 450-454

