$DATUM 2-(4'-Bromophenyl)-7,8-dibromo-1,7,8,8a-tetrahydroazulene-1,1-dicarbonitrile
(10.8). To a stirred solution of DHA 1.8 (679.7 mg, 2.028 mmol) in CH2Cl2
(40 mL) under an argon atmosphere, excluded from light and cooled to -78
°C, was added a solution of Br2 in CH2Cl2 (2.62 mL, 0.78 M, 2.03 mmol)
dropwise. The brown mixture was then stirred for 30 min, after which the
solution took a yellow color. Evaporation of the solvents gave dibromide
10.8. Yellow solid, yield 1.00 g, 2.03 mmol, > 99%. mp 130-150 °C dec. 1H
NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.61 (br s, 4H), 6.97 (s, 1H), 6.29 (dd, J = 7.5,
2.3 Hz, 1H), 6.09 (dd, J = 12.2, 7.5 Hz, 1H), 5.93 (dd, J = 12.2, 5.7 Hz,
1H), 5.33- 5.28 (m, 1H), 5.06-5.02 (m, 1H), 4.65 (s, 1H) ppm. 13C NMR
(125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 144.4, 138.6, 134.7, 132.8, 129.1, 129.0, 127.9,
125.8, 124.9, 121.8, 114.5, 111.6, 53.3, 51.4, 49.1, 44.6 ppm. Anal.
Calcd for C19H14N2Br2 · 0.2 CH2Cl2 (511.99): C, 42.70; H, 2.24; N, 5.47.
Found: C, 43.07; H, 1.87; N, 5.54.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, Br2 added dropwise
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Syntheses of Donor-Acceptor-Functionalized Dihydroazulenes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Broman, Soeren Lindbaek; Jevric, Martyn; Bond, Andrew D.; Nielsen, Mogens
Broendsted
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2014), 79(1), 41-64

