$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
2-(4'-Nitrophenyl)-7,8-dibromo-7,8,1,8a-tetrahydroazulene-1,1-dicarbonitrile
(10.1). To a stirred solution of DHA 1.1 (143 mg, 0.473 mmol) in CH2Cl2
(5 mL) under an argon atmosphere at -78 °C was added a solution of Br2 in
CH2Cl2 (0.61 mL, 0.78 M, 0.47 mmol) dropwise. The brown mixture was then
stirred for 30 min, after which the solution took a yellow color.
Evaporation of the solvents gave dibromide 10.1. Compound 10.28, yield
99%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, Br2 added dropwise
