$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Bromination of alkenols with the H2O2—LiBr—CeIII/CeIV system (general
procedure). To a vigorously stirred solution of alcohol 1a—h (1 mmol),
LiBr, and the CeIII or CeIV salts in water (10 mL), a solution of 35%
H2O2 in water (10 mL) was added by portions of 0.5—0.7 mL within ~4—5 h
at 65—70 °C (reagent ratios are given in Tables 1 and 2). After addition
of the first portion of the H2O2 solution, the reaction mixture turns
pale yellow, the color disappeared after 20—30 min. The reaction mixture
was cooled, extracted with diethyl ether (3x15 mL), the combined organic
layers were washed with water, and dried with MgSO4. The solvent was
removed in vacuo, the yields of the products 2a—h, 3, 4 and the
conversion of alcohol 1a—h were determined by GLC with the internal
standard. The products were isolated by column chromatography.
2,3-Dibromopropan-1-ol (2a), yieldb >99% 1H NMR (CDCl3), δ: 3.78 (m, 2 H,
CH2Br); 3.95 (d, 2 H, CH2OH, J = 8.7 Hz); 4.35 (m, 1 H, CHBr). 13C NMR
(CDCl3), δ: 31.57, 53.36, 64.04. MS, m/z: 217 [M]+ (79Br); 219 [M]+
(81Br).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM selective for vicinal dibromination, no oxidations observed, optimized on
stoichiometry (1:0.3:3:10 reactant:Ce salt:LiBr:H2O2) and temperature,
optimization study, use of Ce(III) nitrate gave same yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
