$DATUM 2-(4'-Tolyl)-7,8-dibromo-7,8,1,8a-tetrahydroazulene-1,1-dicarbonitrile
(10.3). To a stirred solution of DHA 1.3 (560.1 mg, 2.07 mmol) in CH2Cl2
(40 mL) under an argon atmosphere at -78 °C was added a solution of Br2
in CH2Cl2 (2.65 mL, 2.07 mmol, 0.78 M) dropwise. The solution was stirred
for 30 min, after which the solvent was removed in vacuo, which gave
10.3. Dark yellow solid, yield 891 mg, 2.07 mmol, >99%. 1H NMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 7.65 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 2H), 7.28 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 2H), 6.92 (s,
1H), 6.23 (dd, J = 7.6, 2.2 Hz, 1H), 6.08 (dd, J = 12.1, 7.6 Hz, 1H),
5.89 (dd, J = 12.1, 5.6 Hz, 1H), 5.34-5.30 (m, 1H), 5.06-5.03 (m, 1H),
4.64 (br s, 1H), 2.41 (s, 3H) ppm. 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 144.8,
141.0, 140.0, 133.1, 130.2, 128.3, 127.4, 126.4, 126.0, 120.6, 114.8,
111.9, 53.3, 51.7, 49.3, 44.7, 21.6 ppm. Anal. Calcd for C19H14N2Br2
(430.14): C, 53.05; H, 3.28; N, 6.51. Found: C, 52.73; H, 3.05; N, 6.31.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, Br2 added dropwise
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Syntheses of Donor-Acceptor-Functionalized Dihydroazulenes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Broman, Soeren Lindbaek; Jevric, Martyn; Bond, Andrew D.; Nielsen, Mogens
Broendsted
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2014), 79(1), 41-64

