bromine (7.74 mmol, 0.40 mL) in CCl4 (3 mL) was added dropwise over
cinnamonitrile (7.74 mmol, 1.00 mL) in CCl4 (3 mL) at 0 °C and the
resulting mixture was stirred overnight at room temperature. The mixture
was then washed with saturated aqueous Na2S2O5 (2 × 10 mL) and the
aqueous layers were extracted with CH2Cl2 (2 × 10 mL). The combined
organic layers were dried and concentrated in vacuo to obtain
(±)-2,3-dibromo-3-phenylpropanenitrile (2.20 g, 98%).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Enantiopure trans-3-Arylaziridine-2-carboxamides: Preparation by
