$DATUM (1R,2S,3S,6R)-4-(Acetoxymethyl)-6-bromocyclohex-4-ene-1,2,3-triyl
triacetate (15). A cooled (0 °C) solution of 8 (100 mg, 0.290 mmol) in
CH2Cl2 (3 mL) was treated dropwise with phosphorous tribromide (80.0 μL,
0.870 mmol), and the reaction mixture was stirred for 1 h at room
temperature. The reaction mixture was cooled to 0 °C and poured into
saturated NaHCO3 solution and extracted with CH2Cl2 twice. The combined
organic layers were washed with brine, dried over MgSO4, and
concentrated. The residue was purified by column chromatography on silica
gel (hexane/EtOAc, 2:1) to give transposed allylic bromide 15 (116 mg,
98%) as a white solid. mp 68.6-72.5 °C; [α]D 24 +2.3 (c 1.1, CHCl3); 1H
NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz) δ 2.00 (s, 3H), 2.09 (s, 3H), 2.11 (s, 3H), 2.14 (s,
3H), 4.54-4.62 (m, 3H), 5.06 (dd, J = 5.2, 14.8 Hz, 1H), 5.67-5.73 (m,
2H), 6.10 (app t, J = 1.8 Hz, 1H); 1H NMR (CD3OD, 400 MHz) 1.95 (s, 3H),
2.05 (s, 3H), 2.09 (s, 3H), 2.13 (s, 3H), 4.55 (d, J = 13.5 Hz, 1H), 4.64
(d, J = 13.6 Hz, 1H), 4.85 (br d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 5.08 (dd, J = 3.8,
10.9 Hz, 1H), 5.63 (dd, J = 8.1, 10.9 Hz, 1H), 5.71 (d, J = 3.8 Hz, 1H),
6.16 (app t, J = 1.3 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 75 MHz) δ 20.5, 20.69,
20.72 (2C), 45.5, 63.3, 65.3, 69.3, 71.2, 130.2, 131.6, 169.4, 169.8,
170.3 (2C); IR (CHCl3) υmax 2940, 1751, 1371, 1219, 1052 (cm-1); MS (FAB)
(m/z) 429 ([M+23]+, 42), 407 (20), 365 (21), 349 (100), 347 (93); HRMS
(FAB) calcd for C15H19BrO8Na 429.0161 ([M+Na]+), found 429.0146.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
