$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2,3-Dibromo-1-phenylbutane (IIa): Sodium bromide, 20.3 g (0.2 mol), or
potassium bromide, 24 g (0.2 mol), was dissolved in 25 ml of water, and
24 g (0.2 mol) of 33% hydrochloric acid and 13.2 g (0.1 mol) of
(but-2-en-1-yl)benzene (Ia) were added dropwise under stirring over a
period of 30 min. A 18.5% aqueous solution of sodium hypochlorite, 124.2
g (0.2 mol; 110 mol/l of active chlorine) was then added over a period of
90 min, and the mixture was heated to 30-40°C and stirred for 4 h at that
temperature. When the reaction was complete, the organic phase was
separated, washed, and dried over anhydrous calcium chloride. Vacuum
distillation gave IIa. Yield 28.5 g, 98%. bp 130°C (15 mm), d204 =
1.5901, n20D = 1.570; MRD = 60.2, calcd. 60.44. IR spectrum: ν 670 cm-1
(C-Br). 1H NMR spectrum, δ, ppm: 6.71-7.01 m (5H, C6H5), 2.58-2.83 d (2H,
CH2) 3.65-3.68 m (3H, CH), 0.79 s (3H, CH3), 4.01-4.21 m (2H, CHBr).
Found, %: C 40.8; H 4.0; Br 54.66. C12H16Br2. Calculated, %: C 41.1; H
4.1; Br 54.79.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, other product also detected, product depends on
stoichiometry, temperature, KBr/agent also can be used in first stage,
HBr with H2O2/agents also can be used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Hydrogen peroxide- or sodium hypochlorite-induced bromination of
1-arylbut-2-enes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Sadygov, O. A.; Alimardanov, Kh. M.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Russian Journal of Organic Chemistry (2007), 43(11), 1661-1670

