$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 6: 5-((E)-3-Bromoprop-1-enyl)-2-chloropyridine Phosphorous tribromide
(3.95 mL, 42 mmol) was introduced dropwise into a stirred solution of 5
(6 g, 35 mmol) in diethyl ether (350 mL) at 0 °C and the resulting
mixture was allowed to stir for 5 hours. When TLC has shown the full
depletion of the starting material 6, sodium bicarbonate (50 mL) was then
used to quench the reaction. Diethyl ether (5 x 80 mL) was used to
extract the aqueous layer and the combined extracts were washed with
brine (50 mL), dried (MgSO4) and evaporated in vacuo. The crude solid was
purified by flash column chromatography (15:1 hexane/ethyl acetate),
yielding 7.98 g (34 mmol, 98%) of the allylic bromide 19 as a white
solid, where it was then stored immediately as 0.5 M solution in
anhydrous THF. 6: 5-((E)-3-Bromoprop-1-enyl)-2-chloropyridine, yield 7.98
g (34 mmol, 98%) Rf = 0.38 (8:1 hexane/ethyl acetate); 1H NMR (300 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 8.33 (d, J = 2.44 Hz, 1H), 7.66 (dd, J = 8.36, 1.44 Hz, 1H),
7.27 (d, J = 8.36 Hz, 1H), 6.58 (d, J = 16.02 Hz, 1H), 6.42 (m, 1H), 4.11
(dd, J = 0.70, 7.32 Hz, 2H); 13C NMR (75.4 MHz, CDCl3): δ 150.8, 148.2,
135.7, 130.5, 129.3, 128.2, 124.2, 32.0; FTIR (KBr): 1650, 1615, 1501,
1459, 1199, 1098, 970, 816, 580 cm-1; HRMS (EI) Calcd for C8H7BrClN [M+]:
230.9450, found: 230.9448.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Gram-Scale Synthesis of (-)-Epibatidine
