$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Bromine (4.57 mmol, 0.6 Min CH2Cl2) was added to a stirred solution of
acryloylferrocene (1.00 g, 4.17 mmol) in CH2Cl2 at -78°C in 5 min. At the
end of this addition period, the reaction was judged to complete by TLC.
Crude reaction mixture was filtered from a short column using silica gel
and CHCl3 as the eluent. Evaporation of the solvent gave a pure dibromo
compound 2 (1.63 g, 4.08 mmol) in 98% yield.
2,3-dibromopropanoylferrocene (2), (1.63 g, 4.08 mmol) 98% yield.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of new ferrocenyl-substituted aziridines via the
Gabriel-Cromwell reaction
