$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Bromination of alkenols with the
H2O2—LiBr—CeIII/CeIV system (general procedure). To a vigorously stirred
solution of alcohol 1a—h (1 mmol), LiBr, and the CeIII or CeIV salts in
water (10 mL), a solution of 35% H2O2 in water (10 mL) was added by
portions of 0.5—0.7 mL within ~4—5 h at 65—70 °C (reagent ratios are
given in Tables 1 and 2). After addition of the first portion of the H2O2
solution, the reaction mixture turns pale yellow, the color disappeared
after 20—30 min. The reaction mixture was cooled, extracted with diethyl
ether (3x15 mL), the combined organic layers were washed with water, and
dried with MgSO4. The solvent was removed in vacuo, the yields of the
products 2a—h, 3, 4 and the conversion of alcohol 1a—h were determined by
GLC with the internal standard. The products were isolated by column
chromatography. 2,3-Dibromo-3-methylbutan-1-ol (2e), yieldb 98% 1H NMR
(CDCl3), δ: 1.42 (s, 3 H, CH3); 1.44 (s, 3 H, CH3); 3.65 (d, 1 H, CHBr, J
= 8.7 Hz); 4.04 (m, 2 H, CH2OH). 13C NMR (CDCl3), δ: 27.00, 27.16, 34.32,
67.05, 73.08.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM selective for vicinal dibromination, no oxidations observed, yield
depends on amount of LiBr (4 eq. used), use of Ce(IV) ammonium nitrate
gave similar yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Bromination of alkenols with the H2O2-LiBr-CeIII and H2O2-LiBr-CeIV
systems
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Nikishin, G. I.; Sokova, L. L.; Kapustina, N. I.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Russian Chemical Bulletin (2012), 61(2), 459-463

