$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Reaction of II with molecular bromine (ratio
of II:Br2 = 1:1). A mixture of 0.191 g (0.5 mmol) of compound II and
0.080 g (0.5 mmol) of Br2 in 5 ml of CH2Cl2 was kept in the dark for 48 h
at 20°C. The solvent was then evaporated, and the fuming oily residue was
stirred with 1 g (12 mmol) of ZnO in 3 ml of CH2Cl2 for 1 h. The
precipitate was filtered off, the solvent was evaporated, the residue was
chromatographed collecting the fractions with Rf 0.27 and Rf 0.47.
Reaction of II with molecular bromine (ratio of II:Br2= 1:10) was carried
out similarly using a mixture of 0.191 g (0.5 mmol) of compound II and
0.80 g (5 mmol) of Br2. By chromatography the fraction with Rf 0.47 was
isolated.The yield of compound
3,4-Dibromo-1,7-dimethyl-1,7-bis(dichloromethyl)-5,8-ethenodecalin-2,6-dione
(IV), yield 0.27 g (97%). Found, %: C 35.53; H3 .09. C16H16Br2Cl4O2.
Calculated, %: C 35.42, H2.95. .
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, mechanism studied, stage 1 in the dark, alternative
preparation decreased yield, excess bromine used, products depend on
stoichiometry of bromine
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM 1,7-Dimethyl-1,7-dichloromethyl-5,8-ethenodecalin-3-ene-2,6-dione.
