$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Chlorination of
4-aroyl(arylsulfonyl)oxyimino-2-chloro-5-methyl-2,5-cyclohexadienones
IVa-IVg and IVi. Gaseous chlorine was passed at a rate of 15-20 ml/min
through a solution of 0.4 g of compound IVa-IVg or IVi in 3 ml of EtOH,
DMF, or DMF-AcOH (1: 1 or 5:1), heated to 70°C, until saturation. The
mixture was diluted with water, and the precipitate was filtered off and
recrystallized. Compound: VIi (97%). Mp (solvent: AcOH): 160-162°C;
Formula: C13H9Cl3N2O6S.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, Cl gas used at flow rate of 15-20mL/min.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Halogenation of N-Substituted p-Quinonimines and p-Quinone Oxime Esters:
I. Chlorination and Bromination of 4-Aroyloxyimino- and
Arylsulfonyloxyimino-2,5-cyclohexadienones
