$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Chlorination Procedure for Allylic
Alcohols: Potassium hydride (30 % dispersion in mineral oil 1.2 equiv)
was washed with hexane (3 mL) and then a dioxane solution of the allylic
alcohol (1 equiv) was added dropwise. After 5 minutes solid NbCl5 (1.2
equiv) was added as a dry powder. After 10 min1 the reaction mixture was
poured into 2 M HCl and then extracted with ethyl acetate.
2-(Chloromethyl)-3-(3,4-dimethoxyphenyl)acrylonitrile (2j). The general
procedure was employed with
2-((3,4-dimethoxyphenyl)(hydroxy)methyl)acrylonitrile13 (30 mg, 0.14
mmol), potassium hydride (22 mg, 0.17 mmol), niobium pentachloride (46
mg, 1.7 mmol) and dioxane (1 mL) to afford 55 mg (96%) of 2j as an oil.
oil: IR (film) 2212, 1682, 1595, 1513 cm-1; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ
3.93 (s, 6H), 4.32 (s, 2H) 6.70 (d, J= 8.4 Hz, 1H), 7.13 (s, 1H), 7.25
(dd, J= 8.4, 2 Hz, 1H), 7.59 (d, J= 2 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3):
δ 46.4, 55.9, 104.2, 110.4, 110.8, 117.6, 124.5, 125.2, 146.6, 149.0,
151.7; HRMS(ESI) calcd for (M+Na+), C12H13ClNO2 + 238.0631, found
238.0628.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Allylic and Allenic Halide Synthesis via NbCl5- and NbBr5-Mediated
Alkoxide Rearrangements
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Ravikumar, P. C.; Yao, Lihua; Fleming, Fraser F.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2009), 74(19), 7294-7299

