$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 6.3.3 Bromination of 4-tert-butyl cyclohexene (2a) with Br2 in CH2Cl2.
Reagents: 4-tert-butyl cyclohexene (2a) (1 mmol), Br2 (1.25 eq.), CH2Cl2
(10 mL). Mixing of the reagents at 20°C, stirring of the reaction mixture
for 24 h at the same temperature, solvent evaporation and column
chromatography. rel-(1R,3S,4S)-3,4-dibromo-1-tert-butyl cyclohexane (3a),
yield 96%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, alternative reaction conditions gave lower yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Vanadium(V)-Catalyzed Oxidative Bromination of Acid Labile Alkenols and
