$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4,5-Dibromocyclohexene (6)16,18. To a stirred solution of
1,4-cyclohexadiene (35.0 g, 0.44 mol) in hexane (600 mL) was added
dropwise a solution of bromine (70.0 g, 0.44 mol) in hexane (200 mL) at
-45 °C over 4 h. After bromine addition was completed, the mixture was
warmed to r.t. The precipitate was filtered off and discarded.
Evaporation of the solvent under reduced pressure.
4,5-dibromocyclohexene, Yield: 100.3 g (95% isolated yield); white
crystals. mp 34-36 °C (lit. 34-37 °C). 1H NMR (200 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 5.65
(m, 2 H), 4.58 (m, 2 H), 3.17 (dm, A part of AB system, J= 20 Hz), 2.60
(dm, B part of AB system, 2 H, J= 20 Hz). 13C NMR (50 MHz, CDCl3): δ =
124.0, 50.5, 33.0.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
