$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM β-Hexabromo-meso-triphenylsubporphyrin (4a) From subporphyrin 2a (25 mg,
50 μmol), chromatography (CH2Cl2-PE-Et2O, 1:4:1), to give 4a (45.7 mg,
95%) as a yellow solid. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3, -40 °C): δ = 8.12 (d, J =
7.80 Hz, 3 H, o-HPh), 7.75 (t, J = 7.80 Hz, 3 H, m-HPh), 7.70 (t, J =
7.80 Hz, 3 H, p-HPh), 7.51 (t, J = 7.80 Hz, 3 H, m-HPh), 7.25 (d, J =
7.80 Hz, 3 H, o-HPh). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 134.38, 133.08,
132.50, 131.86, 129.34, 127.65, 120.14, 118.42. 19F NMR (376 MHz, CDCl3):
δ = -157.17 (m, 1 F, BF). HRMS (MALDI TOF): m/z [M-F]+ calcd for
C33H15BN3Br6: 936.6490; found: 936.6522. UV/Vis (CH2Cl2): λ (relative
intensity) = 370 (23), 456 (3), 478 nm (1). Fluorescence (CH2Cl2, λex =
370 nm): λmax = 518 nm, ΦF = 0.002.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
