$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4,5-Dibromopentanoic acid (3). A stirring bar, 0.200 g (2.0 mmol) of
4-pentenoic acid and 2.0 mL of dichloromethane were placed into a 4 mL
vial. A PTFE sealed tube filled with 0.11 mL (2.2 mmol) of bromine was
inserted into the solution. Dichloromethane solution was quickly drawn
into the tube. Discoloration of bromine was completed within 5 minutes.
Evaporation of dichloromethane under a reduced pressure gave 0.489 g
(94%) of 4,5-dibromopentanoic acid (3). The crude product gave a
satisfactory 4,5-dibromopentanoic acid (3), yield 0.489 g (94%). 1H NMR
spectrum. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 2.04 (m, 1H), 2.54-2.73 (m, 3H), 3.62
(t, 1H, J = 10.0), 3.87 (dd, J = 10.0, 4.0), 4.25 (m, 1H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
