$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Alkene 1a (0.2 mmol), LiBr (0.4 mmol), NBS
(0.4 mmol), and THF (2.0 mL) were added to a Schlenk tube successively
under an ambient atmosphere. The mixture was stirred at r.t. for the
appropriate time. Sat. aq Na2S2O3 was added to quench the reaction, the
organic layer was washed, then dried over anhyd Na2SO4. Flash column
chromatography gave the pure product 2a. Compound 2b, yield 94%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry-solvent, Schlenk tube used
