$DATUM 7726-95-6
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Brominating (1) and Chlorobrominating (10)
Reagents: Amberlyst A-26, chloride form, is converted to the basic form
by washing with 1 normal aqueous sodium hydroxide solution and then
rinsing with water to neutrality. The resin is then converted to the
bromide form by neutralization with 10% aqueous hydrobromic acid and
dried by azeotropic extraction. This polymer (10 g) is suspended in a 4%
carbon tetrachloride solution of bromine (100 ml) and shaken at room
temperature overnight. The resin is filtered off, washed with carbon
tetrachloride (50 ml), and dried under reduced pressure. The bromine
content is evaluated by extracting a sample of the polymer (1.0 g) with 1
normal aqueous sodium hydroxide and, after acidification, titrating by
iodometry. A mean value of 2.5 mmol bromine/g of polymeric reagent is
obtained for 1. Yield: 94 % cis/trans mixtures: (∼1:3). Reaction
conditions : (solvent/temp/.time): CH2Cl2/reflux/3 h. m.p. or b.p.: 74-77
°C/15 torr.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Anion-exchange resins as halogen carriers in the bromination and
chlorobromination of organic compounds
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Bongini, Alessandro; Cainelli, Gianfranco; Contento, Michele;
Manescalchi, Francesco
