$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
3,4-Dibromo-3,5-dimethyl-tetrahydro-pyran-2-one [(-)-23a and (+)-23b]. To
a solution of (+)-22 (3.7 g, 29.3 mmol) in 20 mL of CH2Cl2 was added Br2
(4.6 mL, 3 equiv) slowly over 10 min at -10 °C (wet ice/acetone bath).
After 2 h at -10 °C, the reaction mixture was slowly poured into a beaker
containing 30 mL of sat. sodium bisulfite and 30 g of ice with aid of
EtOAc with vigorous stirring (the quenching is quite exothermic). The
organic layer was separated, washed with brine, concentrated and
chromatographed (9:1 hexanes:EtOAc) to afford (-)-23a and (+)-23b in the
ratio of 3.7 to 1, both as clear oils that slowly solidified upon
standing to yield crystalline needles (total 5.9 g, 71% yield, well
separated on column, but need not be collected separately).
3,4-Dibromo-3-methyl-dihydro-furan-2-one (40). Under the conditions
similar to those used for (-)-23a, the bromination of 37 (2.5 g, 25.48
mmol) gave 40 (6.1 g, 93% yield) as a white solid: IR (NaCl)
3023.8,1785.8, 1446.4, 1376.9, 1180.2 cm-1; 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ
4.98 (dd, J = 11.7, 3.7 Hz, 1H), 4.84 (d, J = 3.7 Hz, 1H), 4.53 (d, J =
11.1 Hz, 1H), 2.06 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 171.9, 73.8, 54.3,
52.8, 25.3; high resolution mass spectrum (CI+) m/z 256.8817, [(M+H)+,
calcd for C5H7Br2O2 256.8813].
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, scalable
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A Scalable Route to Trisubstituted (E)-Vinyl Bromides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Cho, Cheon-Gyu; Kim, Won-Suk; Smith, Amos B. III
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2005), 7(16), 3569-3572

