$DATUM A solution of 0.5 g of oxime ester Ia, Ib, or Ie in 3 ml of EtOH or DMF
was saturated with chlorine at a flow rate of 15-20 ml/min (50-60°C). The
products were isolated as described. When the reaction was performed in
EtOH, the product precipitated in several hours and was filtered off. The
mixtures obtained in DMF-AcOH were diluted with water, and the
precipitate was filtered off. The products were purified by
recrystallization. The following compound was obtained: in EtOH:
IIa(93%).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, Cl gas used at flow rate of 15-20mL/min.
