$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Bromination of Dimethyl
cis-2,3-dibromo-7-oxabicyclo[2.2.1]hept-5-ene-2,3-dicarboxylate (15) at
77°C. Fifty mg (0.135 mmol) of 15 was dissolved in 15 mL of carbon
tetrachloride. The reaction was carried out as described above. The
solvent was evaporated and residue crystallized from ethylacetate/hexane
(2/1) to give product. Yield: 65 mg (92%) of dimethyl
exo,exo,exo,exo-2,3,5,6-
tetrabromo-7-oxabicyclo[2.2.1]-heptane-2,3-dicarboxylate 16: colorless
crystals. mp. 212-214°C. 1H NMR (200 MHz, CDCl3) δ 5.21 (s, 2H, H5 and
H6), 5.16 (s, 2H, H1 and H4), 3.81 (s, 6H). 13C NMR (50 MHz, CDCl3) δ
168.5, 93.4, 70.2, 56.4, 53.3. IR (KBr, cm-1): 3029, 2978, 2417, 1753,
1548, 1446, 1268, 1217, 1012, 961, 885. C10H10Br4O5; Mr = 529.824,
Monoclinic, P21/n, a = 7.1530 (11) Å, b = 19.1168 (13) Å, c= 10.7770 (12)
Å, β = 102.076 (2) °, Z = 4, 0.20 × 0.20 × 0.15 mm, Prism.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM High-temperature bromination XIII [1]: bromination of dimethyl
7-oxabicyclo[2.2.1]hepta-2,5-diene-2,3-dicarboxylate
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Simsek, Nermin; Arici, Cengiz; McKee, Michael L.; Ulku, Dincer; Balci,
Metin
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Structural Chemistry (2001), 12(3/4), 305-311

